<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:12Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>US Midterms 2026: A history of gerrymandering</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:592df132255233f209feaa6b490f46aeb250c98207303ec58c74108f19c6ab23</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T14:48:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-2026-a-history-of-gerrymandering" /><summary type="html">What does a salamander have to do with US elections? Dating back centuries, gerrymandering continues to play a role in American elections today. Used more often by Republicans in the modern era of voting, Democrats have also resorted to the tactic in the past decade. But what is gerrymandering, and why is it called that? FRANCE 24's Tanishk Saha explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>French President promises 'concrete measures' in response to French students' demands</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5348280ea58e7db7fd37518a3db010d02a9c494bd8331a90e5f4a88507322b44</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T14:39:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-french-president-promises-concrete-measures-in-response-to-french-students-demands" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron said the government would announce “concrete measures" on Monday (October 26) to address school students’ demands after weeks of unrest. Prime Minister Sebastien Lecornu was scheduled to meet with students later Monday. FRANCE 24's Luke Shrago reports from the ground.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterms: Obama blasts Trump's 'chaos and cruelty' while campaigning for Democrats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6969ae6e0d2dbe1139e3f5aa9fa726d4111fcbe517c66d02334af789965e0150</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T14:28:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-obama-blasts-trump-s-chaos-and-cruelty-while-campaigning-for-democrats" /><summary type="html">Ten days out from the elections that will determine control of the closely divided Congress, Barack Obama took to the campaign trail to accuse the Republican president of corruption, deride his strategy for Iran and skewer the gilded aesthetic he has applied ‌to White House renovations. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tens of thousands of Israelis living abroad expected to fly in for pivotal vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d960a0b9f8c15be62df1f40ff3f4c57885fa935acad020af5bec431a3e0c197c</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T14:20:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tens-of-thousands-of-israelis-living-abroad-expected-to-fly-in-for-pivotal-vote" /><summary type="html">Israelis are preparing to head to the polls on Tuesday (October 27). Unable to vote from abroad, tens of thousands of expatriate citizens have been flying in from across the world to cast their ballots. FRANCE 24's Noga Tarnopolsky met some of them at the airport.</summary></entry><entry><title>Serbia's Vucic concedes defeat to the student-led movement: What's next?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e3be2dc575ceb596a36f3d42665c893b00bde8b4a624430976e1e315ae6e702</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T14:12:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/serbia-s-vucic-concedes-defeat-to-the-student-led-movement-what-s-next" /><summary type="html">Serbia's student-led protest movement won a historic victory in parliamentary ⁠election, ending the ​long rule of Aleksandar Vucic and sparking mass celebrations. But their yet-to-be named leaders face a long list of issues. FRANCE 24's Angela Diffley gives us her analysis.</summary></entry><entry><title>Lula wins fourth term: What are the reactions in Brazil?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:24983c18f5431754979991592f0150e978b29294896684dede0fc35871a49d13</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T14:04:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/lula-wins-fourth-term-what-are-the-reactions-in-brazil" /><summary type="html">Brazil's leftist President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva was re-elected against all expectations on Sunday (October 25), but his conservative rival Flavio Bolsonaro refused to accept the loss and said he would seek to have the vote annulled. FRANCE 24's Jan Onoszko tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Bolsonaro's refusal to concede underscores ‘serious’ challenges to Brazil's democratic institutions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:201f7ccee4572a34701e877c70cc14413962e05f652ff05c16259a851fb3002b</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T13:53:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/bolsonaro-s-refusal-to-concede-underscores-serious-challenges-to-brazil-s-democratic-institutions" /><summary type="html">Annette Young is pleased to welcome Dr Pedro Perfeito da Silva, Latin American specialist at the University of Exeter. For Dr Perfeito da Silva, Lula's stunning success reflects the convergence of digital organizing, grassroots mobilization, targeted socioeconomic appeals and an effective effort to mobilise opposition to the Bolsonaro political project. As he explains, Lula assembled a coalition that "not only energized his supporters but also attracted voters from groups that had been somewhat skeptical of the government in the first round."</summary></entry><entry><title>Will Netanyahu's security promise win him this election?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:26227a64a0f2c5de147150d687026283f38ac7a2a08ca56283fe065d3c967ec5</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T13:52:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-will-netanyahu-s-security-promise-win-him-this-election" /><summary type="html">Since the beginning of his political career, Benjamin Netanyahu, Israel's longest-serving prime minister, has campaigned on a promise that he is the only one who will keep the Jewish state safe. As Israelis head to the polls for their first election since the October7 Hamas attacks and the start of the war in Gaza, Netanyahu's strategy might be less effective. FRANCE 24's Gabrielle Nadler explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Lula wins Brazil election but faces uphill battle to govern</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd000ce81ec66d6362c1205dc82824f506bd720a0a2ebd30eb6a8f69e25f6db9</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T13:38:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261026-lula-wins-brazil-election-but-faces-uphill-battle-to-govern" /><summary type="html">Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva's narrow election victory on Sunday has dealt a blow to Brazil's far right, but deep political divisions remain. The newly re-elected president must tackle economic and security concerns at home while navigating international tensions with US President Donald Trump.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Belgrade in rapture as Serbian students topple Vucic in historic election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5bbbdc199bd8091613900e52d57a5231d84ef6a2bcaf613c99c6953fd2e1395b</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T13:19:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-belgrade-in-rapture-as-serbian-students-topple-vucic-in-historic-election" /><summary type="html">Serbia's student-led movement declared victory in parliamentary elections Sunday ending 14 years in power for Aleksandar Vucic's right-wing populist party. Vucic conceded defeat less than two hours after polls closed, triggering raucous scenes in the capital as supporters of the movement celebrated the defeat of a government they blamed for deep-rooted corruption.</summary></entry><entry><title>Live: France will maintain order without state of emergency, but it’s not off the table, Macron says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e94421f24c477cb01e7a85d7612487e58a558ed2ea2d88ed724f9a1e09a9226</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T12:47:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261026-live-france-will-maintain-order-without-state-of-emergency-but-it-s-not-off-the-table-macron-says" /><summary type="html">President Emmanuel Macron on Monday said public order will be maintained in France without the need for a state of emergency, while noting that it was not “off-limits or taboo” if “things were to deteriorate". During a visit to Marseille, Macron promised "concrete" measures to address the demands by high school students after their protests triggered weeks of nationwide unrest. Follow our live blog for all the latest updates.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Israel braces for national elections seen as a referendum on Netanyahu</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b8fd6fad6a9432b994c55c4b7a6682fc778e5c0489d9d27615041917a8f7cb0d</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T12:35:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-braces-for-national-elections-seen-as-a-referendum-on-netanyahu" /><summary type="html">Israelis are preparing to head to the polls on Tuesday (October 27)  in the first elections since the October 7th attacks in 2023. Unable to vote abroad, expatriate citizens have been flying in from around the world to participate in a vote widely seen as being a referendum on Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's leadership.</summary></entry><entry><title>Football: Who will win the 2026 Ballon d'Or?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8d756ab923c58dd917930876422bb9d5a1dea06c5764bf2a16424d0d21a21062</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T12:33:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-football-who-will-win-the-2026-ballon-d-or" /><summary type="html">The competition for this year's Ballon d'Or is tougher than ever. Who will succeed Ousmane Dembélé? Kylian Mbappé, Lamine Yamal and Harry Kane lead a star-studded field. FRANCE 24's Emily Boyle has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Macron vows ‘concrete’ measures to address student demands after unrest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a5b425e40db89903a77f1870ecd914c6fc61e6accf2f463b529a6b83a4d56816</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T12:25:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261026-macron-vows-concrete-measures-to-address-student-demands-after-unrest" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron on Monday said the government will announce "concrete and strong" measures to address the demands by high school students after their protests demanding better education conditions triggered weeks of nationwide unrest. Prime Minister Sébastien Lecornu is set to hold a news conference after meeting with high school student unions.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>French PM meets student representatives after weeks of protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2fc31fbc15edbd0c8bbb5e6b2453130cc51dbbcf8d152b58a1a98df37c1ae53e</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T12:20:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-pm-meets-student-representatives-after-weeks-of-protests" /><summary type="html">French Prime Minister Sebastien Lecornu is set to meet with high school students on Monday afternoon (October 26) to ease tensions in the country after nearly a month of protests. This follows another meeting in which French president Emmanuel Macron promised a concrete response to demands for better education standards and funding.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel: Arab Israeli voters could prove decisive in the upcoming elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:939a10c530e0f9f8016f45b455104d627ec54f2aaa631430dfa35f9bb4e6cf2d</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T12:13:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-arab-israeli-voters-could-prove-decisive-in-the-upcoming-elections" /><summary type="html">In Israel’s election the vote of Arab Israeli citizens could be crucial for the outcome and fate of Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu who is standing for re-election. Traditionally voting turnout is lower among Arab Israelis than among the rest of the population. But this time some feel it’s their duty more than ever to cast their ballot given the policies and wars undertaken by Netanyahu.</summary></entry><entry><title>A look at the main issues in Israeli elections seen as a referendum on Netanyahu</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3ba36443677e782557d0df4f255cd7d3d31c0f8113ef926f53971a804b3c4961</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T11:59:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-a-look-at-the-main-issues-in-israeli-elections-seen-as-a-referendum-on-netanyahu" /><summary type="html">Israelis will vote Tuesday (October 27) in the first national elections since Hamas' Oct. 7, 2023, attack in what is widely seen as a referendum on Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's leadership. He rejected ICC war crimes claims and denied corruption as national elections approach. Details by FRANCE 24's correspondent in Jerusalem, Noga Tarnopolsky.</summary></entry><entry><title>Lula beats Bolsonaro in Brazil runoff: What does it mean for Donald Trump?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:361ad4a685067d269bdd31bba92513f79989ab5f2cc9b154519f543600141f1f</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T11:50:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-lula-beats-bolsonaro-in-brazil-runoff-what-does-it-mean-for-donald-trump" /><summary type="html">Lula defeated on Sunday (October 25) Flavio Bolsonaro in Brazil’s presidential election. But rather than conceding, Bolsonaro called for the result to be annulled. As the US midterms approach, the result raises questions about Trump’s influence and how his political allies respond when voters reject them. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor, Douglas Herbert, gives us his analysis.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterms: Trump's gains among Latino voters in Texas at risk</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6b93469b363335aa1ef4e4a693124aa204c9987acd2d8c9ee1f556dfc7f9b68d</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T11:42:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-us-midterms-trump-s-gains-among-latino-voters-in-texas-at-risk" /><summary type="html">Latino voters shifted toward Trump two years ago, helping him return to the White House with a Republican-controlled Congress. Now, many are souring on the US president and his party. FRANCE 24's team reports from the Rio Grande Valley.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israeli election seen as a referendum: For or against Netanyahu?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:508d82f803b2bda784f04270ce6808ad2d0e929672dcf6bc27332c4414e22fea</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T11:40:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261026-israeli-election-seen-as-a-referendum-for-or-against-netanyahu" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu has led his country almost continuously for nearly 17 years. But will he manage to retain power following Tuesday's election? Netanyahu's latest term has divided Israeli society more than ever and will be marked by the October 7 attacks, his handling of the conflicts in Gaza, Iran and Lebanon, as well as his controversial judicial reform. FRANCE 24's David Gilberg reports, with Lauren Bain.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>'An everyday habit': 2.5 billion lines of cocaine snorted in England per year</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9dd9c78d6b4d3dd7d6400fc15cbdeff1d44754b3caffa55bd0e124c539107e62</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T11:05:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261026-an-everyday-habit-2-5-billion-lines-of-cocaine-snorted-in-england-per-year" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Monday, October 26: Brazilian and international papers react to Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva's presidential election victory. Next: The New York Times warns that the war in Iran is entering a dangerous new phase. Also: cocaine consumption and cocaine-related crimes are surging across Britain. Finally, it turns out that wrapping children in cotton wool isn't the best parenting strategy.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Algeria to send troops to Niger in first foreign deployment in over 50 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a2ed53c26c132c1eff8603e8be793cecf06caa69ba4b0b5f151f9247e6f34cfe</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T10:10:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261026-algeria-to-send-troops-to-niger-in-first-foreign-deployment-in-over-50-years" /><summary type="html">Algeria’s parliament on Sunday approved a resolution to send troops to Niger, making the first time Algerian soldiers will be deployed abroad since the 1973 Arab-Israeli war. Niger faces persistent attacks by armed groups, including near its border with Algeria, and the deployment comes as Algiers and Niamey are building the Trans-Saharan Gas Pipeline after decades of delays.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>'Serbia is free': Belgrade erupts in celebration after Vucic's defeat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d09a8b859f25d70bda25db53c847ebb3b635a250ba492a96582c9f863f15e25</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T09:55:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/serbia-is-free-belgrade-erupts-in-celebration-after-vucic-s-defeat" /><summary type="html">Celebrations erupted across several Serbian cities late Sunday (October 25) as people hailed the student-backed movement deposing veteran leader Aleksandar Vucic's party in a snap election.</summary></entry><entry><title>Brazil: What challenges await Lula in his fourth term as president?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c7cd5915559ce519dcf9f3edb98f1acccba6157b01a1e7d4600155a1840032c3</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T09:46:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-what-challenges-await-lula-in-his-fourth-term-as-president" /><summary type="html">Brazilian President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva, nearly 81 years old, clinched a fourth term in a tight runoff against Flavio Bolsonaro on Sunday (October 25). He will have to wrestle with a divided Brazil, an unfriendly Congress, feeble public finances and a Donald Trump-shaped menace during his unprecedented fourth term.</summary></entry></feed>
